.TH MOTDER 1 "2026-10-04" "motder 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
motder \- add, list and dismiss messages in Ubuntu's message of the day
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B motder
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B motder
manages a list of administrator messages that are shown in the dynamic
message of the day at login. It installs a single hook,
.IR /etc/update-motd.d/99-motder ,
which
.BR pam_motd (8)
runs at login along with Ubuntu's other update-motd scripts.
.PP
Messages are numbered from 1 (oldest) in the order they were added.
Numbers are positions in the current list and shift after a dismissal.
.PP
Changing messages requires root. Listing works for any user.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "add " MESSAGE ...
Add a message. Words are joined with single spaces. If no
.I MESSAGE
is given, or it is
.BR \- ,
the message is read from standard input and may span several lines.
.TP
.BR list ", " ls " [" \-\-json ]
List messages with their index and age. This is the default command.
.B \-\-json
prints a JSON array with
.IR index ,
.IR id ,
.I created
(RFC 3339, UTC) and
.IR text .
.TP
.BR dismiss ", " rm " [\fIINDEX\fR]..."
Dismiss the messages with the given indices. With no index, dismiss the
last (most recently added) message. If any index is invalid, nothing is
dismissed.
.TP
.B clear
Dismiss all messages.
.TP
.B show
Print the text motder contributes to the login screen.
.TP
.B install
Install or repair the hook. Every change does this automatically.
.TP
.BR uninstall " [" \-\-purge ]
Remove the hook. Messages are kept unless
.B \-\-purge
is given.
.TP
.B help
Show usage information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " DIR"
Directory holding the messages. Default:
.IR /var/lib/motder .
.TP
.BI \-\-motd\-dir " DIR"
The update-motd script directory. Default:
.IR /etc/update-motd.d .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat all following arguments as message text, for messages that begin
with a dash.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MOTDER_STATE_DIR
Default for
.BR \-\-state\-dir .
.TP
.B MOTDER_MOTD_DIR
Default for
.BR \-\-motd\-dir .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/motder/messages
The stored messages.
.TP
.I /var/lib/motder/motd
The rendered text printed at login.
.TP
.I /etc/update-motd.d/99-motder
The hook script.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 on invalid usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo motder add 'Maintenance window: Saturday 02:00\-04:00 UTC'
df \-h /data | sudo motder add
motder list
sudo motder dismiss
sudo motder dismiss 1 3
sudo run\-parts /etc/update\-motd.d    # preview the full motd
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR update\-motd (5),
.BR pam_motd (8),
.BR run\-parts (8)
